  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "Spatial imbalance metrics serve only as a proxy diagnostic tool and do not directly measure or prove energy injustice on their own.",
      "what": "The authors introduce a method based on the energyshed concept to map spatial supply and demand relationships between urban energy-consuming areas and power generation facilities. The framework calculates geographical energy balances and identifies specific generation sources for cities without requiring localized distance thresholds or proprietary algorithms.",
      "why": "It creates an open technique for pinpointing regions that absorb environmental and operational burdens to power distant cities, establishing a spatial diagnostic tool for energy justice policies."
    }
